      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm seeing some issues in our GKE production cluster. one of our microservices is stuck in CrashLoopBackOff. here are the logs from the last few restarts:\n\n[error] container_image_pull_backoff: failed to pull image \"prod-registry.io/auth-service:v2.4.1\"\n[error] liveness probe failed: Get \"http://10.128.0.5:8080/health\": dial tcp 10.128.0.5:8080: connect: connection refused\n[status] back-off restarting failed container\n\ncan u give me a checklist of what to check to figure out if this is a resource issue, probe config, or something else? we need to stabilize this ASAP.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
